        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Co2(OH2)(piv)4(Hpiv)4 (0.09 g, 0.09 mmol) and Dy(NO3)3·xH2O (0.054 g, 0.15 mmol) were dissolved in 10 mL of acetonitrile, followed by addition of C4-H2dea (0.055 g, 0.40 mmol) and triethylamine (0.06 g, 0.60 mmol) in 10 mL of acetonitrile, affording a purple solution. The mixture was stirred for 1 h, filtered, and allowed to stand sealed at room temperature. Within 3–4 weeks violet crystals suitable for SCXRD formed; remaining crystals were filtered, washed with acetonitrile and air dried.",
